<%# The options behind every picker on this page.

    ONE COPY, by id. A funnel form holds up to eight pickers over the same
    couple of hundred paths; rendering the list into each field would put the
    same tens of kilobytes on the page nine times. See OffersKnownValues.

    Split from the sentence that explains it (see _known_values_note) because a
    custom dashboard needs the two in different places: the payload sits on the
    dashboard, where it is loaded once, while the note belongs inside the one
    widget panel that happens to be open.

    `json_escape` rather than trusting the JSON encoder's escaping config: these
    strings are paths and event names from a customer's website, they are going
    inside a <script> element, and a literal "</script>" in one of them would
    end the element early and put the rest of the payload into the document as
    markup. escape_html_entities_in_json defaults to on and would also prevent
    that, but it is an application-wide setting that something else could turn
    off, and this is not a decision that should be reachable from an initializer. -%>
<%= tag.script json_escape(known_values.payload.to_json).html_safe,
               type: "application/json",
               id: OffersKnownValues::KNOWN_VALUES_DOM_ID %>
